{"title":"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Asima and Nile each think of an integer greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Each of them performs the following operations on their integer: they double it, then subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and then multiply it by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The sum of their results is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/b/b7bac8d158ad07b42ad9889011a7e4e67851a82d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$440$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. How many possibilities are there for Asima’s original integer?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/0/090733e4907c53143df99f5a6ad5de6fb9713707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 64 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 44 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 65 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 45 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/8/7b86f59943b2c1311be46930f335369f85c0192f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = (2x - 10) \\times 4 = 8(x - 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"256\" height=\"20\" /> represent the output when the starting number is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be Asima's number, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be Nile's number. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/3/d43fee4bc8ea93e30d27ad7240eb20d3d90f58b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a) + f(n) = 440$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e04fd5699f0ddb3b5905ff08eb52ffe254cab4a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8(a - 5) + 8(n - 5) = 440$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdec457c26d6586e1df2fed7926de59a7d549f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8(a - 5) + 8(n - 5)}{8} = \\frac{440}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"213\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/0/c004109aa02508a50f9dccbc06060edf39fc404a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a - 5 + n - 5 = 55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"150\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b35c34fb4a8da3b830a816e9cd4702d994c3b8e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + n - 10 = 55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65edf233d849ad4fab2f8eba7ab392a38ffafb15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + n = 55 + 10 = 65$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"170\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Since each of their numbers are integers and must be positive, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> can be any value from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> cannot go above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> because then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or lower. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/a/5ea120dff048934af51abf89df1b71e6e90d1c9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } 64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a 